{"slug":"/students/subjects/chemistry/nuclear-chemistry/radioactivity/","source":"students/subjects/chemistry/nuclear-chemistry/radioactivity.html","area":"students","kind":"content","title":"Radioactivity — Nuclear Chemistry","description":"","subject":"chemistry","body":"<div class=\"max-w-4xl mx-auto\">\n    <nav class=\"mb-6\"><a href=\"/students/subjects/chemistry/nuclear-chemistry/\" class=\"text-blue-600\">← Back to Division 11</a></nav>\n\n    <main class=\"content-card p-6 rounded-xl\">\n      <h1 class=\"text-2xl font-bold mb-2\">Radioactivity: Types &amp; Properties</h1>\n      <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-4\">Overview of alpha, beta and gamma emissions, half-life and detection.</p>\n\n      <h3 class=\"font-semibold mt-4\">Worked example</h3>\n      <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-800\">If a sample has a half-life of 5 years, after 15 years what fraction remains? Answer: (1/2)^(15/5) = (1/2)^3 = 1/8.</p>\n\n      <h3 class=\"font-semibold mt-4\">Practice</h3>\n      <ol class=\"list-decimal pl-5 text-gray-800\">\n        <li>Define half-life and calculate remaining fraction after two half-lives.</li>\n      </ol>\n    </main>\n  </div>\n<!-- Topic Quiz System -->","bodyClass":"min-h-screen bg-gradient-to-br from-purple-50 to-pink-50 p-6","bodyStyle":"","css":["body{font-family:Inter, sans-serif}.content-card{ -webkit-backdrop-filter:blur(12px);backdrop-filter:blur(12px);background:rgba(255,255,255,0.7);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.2);box-shadow:0 8px 32px rgba(0,0,0,0.06);}"],"quiz":null,"tracker":null,"links":[]}